	(text "Budget: +5V <= 1 A (TSR 1-2450), +3V3 <= 1 A (AP7361C, ~0.85 W at 0.5 A -> copper pour on tab).\nVBUS from USB-C on the MCU sheet: logic can be flashed without +24V, relays stay off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 88.138 55.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cb1691c1-2374-40b7-ad7b-5d82a24e194f")
	)
	(text "Power\n+24V (L+ from PL1) -> buck -> +5V -> LDO -> +3V3. GND = L-.\nRails are power symbols (global), so this block has no sheet pins."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ee4ce8d0-0219-4784-92ee-93dbe93bb9b9")
	)
	(text_box "TO DESIGN\n- Input +24V (L+) from the PL1 regulator 1U1 (LM350K). Load from this board: up to ~8 relay coils at ~20 mA + logic = approx. 0.4 A peak at 24 V.\n  Check the spare capacity of 1U1 next to the existing PL1 loads (Signal_list V6).\n- Input protection: resettable fuse, TVS, bulk capacitor.\n- +5V for display backlight and USB; +3V3 for ESP32-S3 (Wi-Fi peaks ~0.5 A), MAX31865 and opto pull-ups.\n- USB VBUS diode-ORed onto +5V: the logic can be programmed without the chamber powered (relays stay off without +24V).\n- Test points on every rail.\n\nCOMPONENT PROPOSAL\n- +5V: Traco TSR 1-2450 (1 A, 6.5-36 V in, drop-in switching regulator module - no layout risk).\n- +3V3: LDO from +5V, Diodes AP7361C-33E (1 A, SOT-223) - so USB alone can power the logic.\n- Input: PTC 0.5 A hold >= 30 V (1812), TVS SMBJ33CA, 100 uF / 50 V electrolytic + 10 uF / 50 V ceramic.\n- ORing: 2x SS34 Schottky (VBUS and regulator output)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 127 12.7 0)
		(size 154.94 38.1)
		(margins 1.0287 1.0287 1.0287 1.0287)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3d2e39b4-9be9-4671-8b69-956be3e85bb2")
	)
